      en: "Dong Phou Vieng National Park is located in the central province of Savannakhet, covering an expansive area of 1,970 square kilometers. The protected landscape consists primarily of mixed dry dipterocarp and evergreen forests rolling across relatively gentle, hilly terrain. It is a vital sanctuary for several highly endangered species, offering refuge to the silvered leaf monkey (langur), giant pangolins, hornbills, and clouded leopards. Beyond its ecological significance, the park is deeply intertwined with cultural heritage, as it is the traditional homeland of the Katang ethnic minority. Sustainable ecotourism initiatives here allow visitors to undertake multi-day treks, combining wildlife spotting with authentic cultural immersions in animist Katang villages."
